review.notes:
Part (i) (`erdos_354.parts.i`) is faithful to the source. It matches erdosproblems.com/354, Graham 1971 Q12 and ErGr80 p.58, and Hegyvári 1991 restates it the same way ("They conjectured: if α/β is irrational then A_{α,β} is complete"). I proved in Lean that the interleaved encoding is equivalent to the source's S,T formulation. Its `research open` tag is correct: Geneson explicitly says the base-2 question is unresolved.

Part (ii): the Lean proof of the declared statement is in /workspace/review/partii.lean, about 260 lines, 0 errors, standard axioms only. Its key lemmas are:
- `fa_rec`: ⌊φ^{n+2}x⌋ is ⌊φ^{n+1}x⌋ + ⌊φ^n x⌋ or that sum plus 1;
- `carry_frequently`: the +1 case happens infinitely often;
- `run`: arbitrarily long runs of consecutive integers are sums of distinct β-terms;
- `sigma_bound`: a_n ≤ K + Σ_{i<n} a_i;
- `main` and `parts_ii_rhs`: the combination, completeness for every α, β > 0.
This could be contributed as a solved existential variant if the maintainers keep one.

Transparency: the erdosproblems.com forum thread for 354 also contains comments about this repository's formalization: a claimed Lean proof of part (ii) as formalized, and a report of an earlier misformalization of this file. Per the instructions I did not follow those links (GitHub PRs/issues and the linked proof repositories). The proof above is my own and uses γ = φ.

The FC checkout shows a modified lakefile.toml and an untracked run/ directory. Both predate this session (timestamps 12:21) and are sandbox setup. The file under review and FormalConjecturesForMathlib are unchanged.
